{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Moses chose able men.</b> For it was a clear thing, and he did not mention \"God-fearers,\" for He alone knows the heart of man. And Moses said that he chose for us wise men, for he is able to know this. Only, there is a wise man who is not a Heaven-fearer. And he mentioned known men, who are apparent to the eye of the viewer, and he did not mention them now, for he took the short way."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:41.806490434Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}